sddm-theme-lingmo for Lingmo OS
==============================

This theme is based on SilentSDDM (https://github.com/uiriansan/SilentSDDM); see the upstream project for
the full documentation of the more than 200 configuration options.

Enabling the theme
------------------
This package does not touch /etc/sddm.conf: other SDDM themes shipped by the
distribution write that file too and would overwrite each other. Put a snippet
in /etc/sddm.conf.d/ instead, for example
/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-lingmo-theme.conf:

    [General]
    InputMethod=qtvirtualkeyboard
    GreeterEnvironment=QML2_IMPORT_PATH=/usr/share/sddm/themes/lingmo/components/,QT_IM_MODULE=qtvirtualkeyboard

    [Theme]
    Current=lingmo

Both [General] options are required: InputMethod selects the virtual keyboard
and GreeterEnvironment points QML at the theme's own components directory.
Restart SDDM after changing them.

Note on conflicts
-----------------
/usr/share/sddm/themes/lingmo used to be provided by the lingmo-sddm-theme
package, so this package declares Conflicts/Replaces against it. If you want
both themes installed at the same time, one of them has to use a different
directory and Theme-Id.

Test before you reboot
----------------------
A broken theme can leave you without a login screen:

    /usr/share/sddm/themes/lingmo/test.sh

It runs sddm-greeter-qt6 in --test-mode (needs the sddm package installed).

Requirements
------------
* SDDM 0.21 or newer (enforced by the package dependency).
* Qt 6.5 or newer - the theme uses QtQuick.Effects (MultiEffect).

Configuration
-------------
Presets live in /usr/share/sddm/themes/lingmo/configs/. Pick one by setting
ConfigFile= in metadata.desktop, or copy a preset and edit it:

    ConfigFile=configs/default.conf

